  VALUES
    ('housing', 2, 'Beaty called housing a ''fundamental human right'' in her 2023 State of the City address. She secured $9 million from the Metro Affordable Housing Bond for the Amity Orchards complex (164 affordable units), championed $850,000 in ARPA funds for affordable housing, and led Beaverton to be named a global finalist in the 2025 Bloomberg Mayors Challenge for an innovative cooperative housing model. As a councilor she worked on the regional housing coalition to build more affordable housing. This consistent record of publicly funding new affordable housing and requiring affordability in developments maps to Chair 2.', ARRAY['https://beavertonvalleytimes.com/2026/05/30/beaverton-metro-cuts-the-ribbon-on-multigenerational-affordable-housing-complex-amity-orchards/', 'https://beavertonvalleytimes.com/2025/07/20/beaverton-named-global-finalist-in-bloomberg-mayors-challenge-for-innovative-housing-plan/', 'https://www.governing.com/urban/oregon-city-explores-new-ways-to-develop-senior-housing']::text[]),
